Subject: Game controllers: a fixed built-in scheme next to the keyboard and
 mouse

The first game controller SDL knows plays, with no setup (a DualShock 3 is
"PS3 Controller", whatever its raw button numbers); the old joystick code
was never built (WITH_JOYSTICK is defined nowhere). Its buttons become the
keys the game already reads, so the menus, the level end and the
game-over screen work as with the keyboard:

  left stick       move the ship (as the mouse, the old joystick smoothing)
  D-pad            move (the arrow keys); in the menus up/down/left/right
  Cross, R1        fire (Space); in the menus select
  Square, L1       use the item (Return)
  Triangle         next item (')
  Start            the menu, and back to the game from it (Escape)
  Circle           back to the game from the menu (Escape)

A controller plugged in later is taken when none is open; an unplugged one
releases the trigger and the next one present takes over.

Forwarded: not-needed

